---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Contact · Where to Apply" description="Contact the maintainer of Where to Apply about corrections, suggestions, or the project.">
  <main class="wrap py-16 md:py-24">
    <a class="link text-sm" href="/">← Where to Apply</a>
    <h1 class="mt-8 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Contact</h1>
    <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
      <p>Where to Apply is maintained by Hardikk Kamboj. If you find an outdated job board, a broken company careers link, a useful community that should be listed, or a problem with how the site works, please send the details so the directory can be corrected.</p>
      <p>The most useful way to report a source change is through the <a class="link" href="https://github.com/khardikk/where-to-apply/issues">project issue tracker</a>. Include the source name, its current URL, and the replacement URL or evidence for the correction. You can also propose additions there; please explain which roles or locations the source serves and why it is useful to job seekers.</p>
      <p>For code contributions, review the repository's contribution guide and open a pull request. Security concerns should be reported using the process in the repository's SECURITY.md file rather than in a public issue. General project information and updates are available from <a class="link" href="https://hardikk.dev">Hardikk's website</a> and <a class="link" href="https://x.com/HdKamboj">X profile</a>.</p>
      <p>Where to Apply does not recruit for the companies listed and cannot answer questions about an employer's open role, application status, or hiring decision. Contact the employer directly for those matters. See the <a class="link" href="/privacy">privacy page</a> for information about this website.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
